I have a bone to pick.

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:29.429 size:84% position:42%
-I think we could admit
I drank more than you.

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:32.932 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I understand I drank less
than anybody ever drank

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:34.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
on "Day Drinking
with Seth Meyers,"

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:37.537 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I need a redo.
[ Laughs ]

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:40.373 size:88% position:44%
And none of those little
shot glasses, you know?

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:41.908 line:92%
I'm bringing my own glass.

00:00:41.908 --> 00:00:43.443 line:92%
-Well, I notice you posted this.

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:44.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, my God! There!
Thank you for showing that

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:46.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's what I'm bringing.
[ Laughs ]

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:48.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
-'Cause I saw that you
posted this on social media,

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:50.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was like,
"Where was this Ina...

00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:51.618 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:53.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...when we were
drinking it up?"

00:00:53.286 --> 00:00:56.589
-Now it should be noted,
you drank less than I did,

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:58.058 line:92%
but, you know, a lot of your -

00:00:58.058 --> 00:00:59.692 align:start size:94% position:6%
at the time,
people you worked with,

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:01.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
some of your colleagues
were there, and they did say

00:01:01.661 --> 00:01:03.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
it was the drunkest
they'd ever seen you,

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:05.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
so you did have something.
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:05.165 --> 00:01:06.900 size:75% position:38%
-That was something.
And I have to say --

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was very drunk.
And I just want to show

00:01:08.435 --> 00:01:10.003 align:start size:94% position:6%
everybody how supportive
a friend you are.

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:13.339 size:81% position:41%
Look at that lovely --
just a hand on my arm,

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:16.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
being like, "There, there.
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:16.443 --> 00:01:17.744 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-"It'll be over soon."

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:20.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I do remember
you trying to decorate a cake.

00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:21.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-It wasn't pretty.

00:01:21.581 --> 00:01:23.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Let's try to --
I don't think we need to

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:27.220 align:start size:94% position:6%
remind everybody how badly -
-It was so much fun.

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:28.688 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was just great.
-It was a blast.

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:30.890 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is --
This is a lovely book.

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:31.891 size:88% position:44% line:92%
A book that was planned.

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:34.094 align:start size:94% position:6%
The idea of food as comfor
is comfort food.

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:35.528
It was planned for the election.
-Yeah.

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:37.630 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You did not know that it woul
also be coming back

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:39.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
when people,
during a pandemic,

00:01:39.299 --> 00:01:40.667 align:start size:94% position:6%
might want to find
comfort in food.

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:41.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it's a well-timed book,
unfortunately.

00:01:41.835 --> 00:01:44.037 size:81% position:41%
-And all the layers --
I mean, the pandemic

00:01:44.037 --> 00:01:47.707
and racial justice and all
the issues that are going on

00:01:47.707 --> 00:01:49.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
everybody is
so completely stressed.

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:52.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's amazing.
It really is crazy.

00:01:52.312 --> 00:01:54.280 size:84% position:42%
-And I think, you know,
when you're stressed

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:55.148 line:92%
and yet you also want to cook,

00:01:55.148 --> 00:01:58.284
maybe now is not the time fo
more experimental cooking.

00:01:58.284 --> 00:02:02.188
Maybe now's the time to sort o
cook the sort of recipes in here

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:04.257 align:start size:94% position:6%
that are the food
you're familiar with

00:02:04.257 --> 00:02:06.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
that have sort of
simpler preparation.

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:09.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, what are your favorit
comfort foods?

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:12.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean,
you know, mashed potatoes.

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:13.133 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:15.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, baked chicken,
stuff like that.

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:18.872 size:84% position:42%
-I have mashed potatoes
with lemon zest in it,

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:20.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the book, that's so good.
-See?

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:23.977 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you know what else?
Emily Blunt gave me a recipe

00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:27.380
for her roast potatoes
that you actually cook --

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:29.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
parboil and then
you let them dry out.

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:33.219 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then you toss them with oi
and bake them,

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:36.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they are so crisp
on the outside,

00:02:36.022 --> 00:02:38.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the inside,
they're like mashed potatoes

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:39.526 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
They're amazing.

00:02:39.526 --> 00:02:43.263 align:start size:94% position:6%
So if you like mashed potatoes
you'll be gone on this one

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:44.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I didn't know
this about Emily Blunt.

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:46.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
I didn't know that people were
allowed to just pitch...

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:49.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She's a great cook.
-...pitch recipes to you.

00:02:49.269 --> 00:02:51.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
It feels like,
based on our friendship,

00:02:51.004 --> 00:02:52.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
you should've asked
if I had any.

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:55.241 size:78% position:39%
-You know how it is.
Trade makeup secrets.

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:56.209 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Both laugh ]

00:02:56.209 --> 00:02:58.011 size:84% position:42%
-Hey, one of the things
a lot of people cooked

00:02:58.011 --> 00:03:00.213
that I think they thought
would bring them comfort

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:01.948 align:start size:94% position:6%
and maybe didn't
during this pandemic,

00:03:01.948 --> 00:03:04.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, obviously,
much has been written about it

00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:07.020 align:start size:94% position:6%
are sourdough --
the sourdough starter.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:09.989 size:78% position:39%
How do you feel like
this trend will last?

00:03:09.989 --> 00:03:13.126
-I can't tell you how many
people e-mailed me and said,

00:03:13.126 --> 00:03:15.028 size:84% position:42%
"What should I do about
the sourdough starter?"

00:03:15.028 --> 00:03:19.132
And I'm like, "I've never made a
sourdough bread in my life."

00:03:19.132 --> 00:03:20.867 line:92%
So I had to make stuff up.

00:03:20.867 --> 00:03:23.436 size:84% position:42%
I think it's gonna last
for about five minutes.

00:03:23.436 --> 00:03:25.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-It was maybe the first week

00:03:25.305 --> 00:03:27.273 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the pandemic
I got a lot of questions.

00:03:27.273 --> 00:03:29.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
After that, nothing.
Radio silence.

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:32.679
-My takeaway is, it is -- I've
always been a fan of sourdough

00:03:32.679 --> 00:03:34.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then you try to make one
and you're like,

00:03:34.314 --> 00:03:36.249 line:92%
"This is a pretty needy bread.

00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:38.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, it wants
a lot of attention."

00:03:38.284 --> 00:03:40.520 size:84% position:42%
-Everyone is different.
You know, do you start

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:43.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
with the starter or do you get
the free yeasts in the air

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:46.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, like, how about
go to the bakery

00:03:46.392 --> 00:03:49.028 size:84% position:42%
and get sourdough bread
and have a good time?

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:51.297 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Absolutely.
And I think, you know,

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:55.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
now is a good time, obviously,
if you can, if it's safe,

00:03:55.068 --> 00:03:57.804
it's really important to g
to things like bakeries to

00:03:57.804 --> 00:03:59.005 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, support restaurants.
-Yeah.

00:03:59.005 --> 00:04:02.442 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is a really hard time.
How do you feel like

00:04:02.442 --> 00:04:05.545
this time that we're livin
through has reminded peopl

00:04:05.545 --> 00:04:08.281 align:start size:94% position:6%
the importance their
relationship to food has,

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:10.516 align:start size:94% position:6%
insofar that it supports
your relationship

00:04:10.516 --> 00:04:12.051 line:92%
with your friends and family

00:04:12.051 --> 00:04:14.654 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, you know,
the thing that happened was,

00:04:14.654 --> 00:04:16.089 size:84% position:42% line:92%
everything was so busy.

00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:17.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
Everybody was running around
like crazy.

00:04:17.757 --> 00:04:19.993 size:75% position:38%
And all of a sudden,
it was just stopped.

00:04:19.993 --> 00:04:23.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was quiet.
And I think we really got back

00:04:23.363 --> 00:04:24.163 line:92%
to the stuff that was important,

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:27.867
which is cooking and taking care
of the people around us,

00:04:27.867 --> 00:04:28.935 size:88% position:44% line:92%
maybe roasting something

00:04:28.935 --> 00:04:31.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
and leaving it
at a neighbor's house.

00:04:31.337 --> 00:04:33.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was -- I think we got bac
to what we really

00:04:33.773 --> 00:04:36.509 align:start size:94% position:6%
used to love doing,
and it was simple.

00:04:36.509 --> 00:04:40.179
I mean, I had a dinner party
the other night, and, literally,

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:44.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had no time to cook,
so I got pizzas from Sam's

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:47.920
in East Hampton, which is great,
and I set a great table,

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:49.422 line:92%
and we sat out under the stars

00:04:49.422 --> 00:04:53.126
and it was a gorgeous night with
a big fire in the fire bowl.

00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:56.062 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we had a wonderful time,
and that's all we need.

00:04:56.062 --> 00:04:58.298 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, it doesn't have to b
some big fancy dinner

00:04:58.298 --> 00:05:02.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
with octopus eyeballs and foam
[ Laughs ]

00:05:02.435 --> 00:05:04.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-It just needs to be something

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:06.906 size:75% position:38%
where you're sharing
something together

00:05:06.906 --> 00:05:07.940 line:92%
and you have a good time.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:10.643 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Something we shared
during this time was that

00:05:10.643 --> 00:05:14.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
we both produced our shows
remotely, by ourselves.

00:05:14.947 --> 00:05:16.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
Basically,
we were the full staff.

00:05:16.983 --> 00:05:18.918 align:start size:94% position:6%
How did you find that time
-Wasn't that fun?

00:05:18.918 --> 00:05:20.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughs ]
-It's fun to be back

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:23.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
around people that know
what they're doing.

00:05:23.523 --> 00:05:24.857 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:24.857 --> 00:05:26.626 line:92%
-Well, you had Alexi, right?

00:05:26.626 --> 00:05:28.428 line:92%
-Alexi was not that helpful.

00:05:28.428 --> 00:05:29.929 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-Well, I don't even have Alexi

00:05:29.929 --> 00:05:32.498 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She doesn't watch the show,
so she didn't really know

00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:34.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
what we were aiming for.
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:36.436 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I feel safe
to say this about her

00:05:36.436 --> 00:05:39.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
with the confidence
that she'll never see this

00:05:39.706 --> 00:05:42.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
Yes.

00:05:42.141 --> 00:05:43.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you didn't
have to cook food.

00:05:43.376 --> 00:05:44.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's true, that's true.
-I had to do my hair.

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:46.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I should take a big step back
and make sure that's clear

00:05:46.612 --> 00:05:50.083
-I was the food stylist, the
prop stylist, the mic person

00:05:50.083 --> 00:05:54.487
I wasn't very good at the mic.
I used to forget to turn it on

00:05:54.487 --> 00:05:56.389 line:92%
I had two iPhones as cameras

00:05:56.389 --> 00:05:58.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had to set them up,
the detail shot.

00:05:58.725 --> 00:06:00.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I had to --
I was exhausted.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:02.862 line:92%
Then I had to be the presenter

00:06:02.862 --> 00:06:04.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was -- [ Laughs ]
-Yes.

00:06:04.397 --> 00:06:05.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was hard.
-You had a far --

00:06:05.832 --> 00:06:11.471
Now that you mention it, a far
far higher bar than I had, so...

00:06:11.471 --> 00:06:12.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, and then
I had to do the dishes.

00:06:12.672 --> 00:06:13.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
You didn't have to do
the dishes.

00:06:13.773 --> 00:06:15.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, I didn't
have to do the dishes.

00:06:15.274 --> 00:06:17.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now I am worried
my wife's gonna see this,

00:06:17.176 --> 00:06:19.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I'll just say
I love you, babe.

00:06:19.178 --> 00:06:21.013 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:21.013 --> 00:06:22.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's always such a pleasur
to see you, Ina.

00:06:22.582 --> 00:06:24.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
Congratulations on the book.
-Thank you, thank you.

00:06:24.317 --> 00:06:27.186 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I can't wait to see you
in person again soon.

00:06:27.186 --> 00:06:29.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was really fun.
Okay, great to see you.

00:06:29.055 --> 00:06:30.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
Stay safe.
-Great to see you, too.

00:06:30.089 --> 00:06:32.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Modern Comfort Food"
is available now.

